      "drill grid 0.01 mm is mine (a fab usually offers 0.05 steps: 0.35 and 0.65); configurable",
      "one bigger via per net is expected; several minimum vias in parallel (sum of circumferences, power-via rule 2) would also carry 1.0 mm (2 x 0.785 = 1.57) - not drawn, the 5.4 text asks for 'the smallest drill with pi x drill >= width'",
      "each net has one pad on F.Cu and one on B.Cu, so exactly one via is topologically required per net; the via sits mid-row (any x clear of the pads gives the same length)",
      "the 2.0 mm HEAVY trace is an extreme to show the rule scales; a via annulus narrower than the trace is accepted (the circumference criterion, not the diameter, is the rule)"
    ],
